            "review_title": "Review at Quán Cô Hồng - Đặc Sản Đà Nẵng",
            "review_text": "Ray Ray Ray\nDubai, United Arab Emirates936 contributions\n0\nAn unfortunate tourist trap where the marketing does not meet reality.\nSep 2022 • Friends\nPhotos in the menu are very different than what was presented (-1 point)\n\nDepth and flavour of recipes do not represent good quality dac san. The restaurant which is well appointed does not have the same level of execution. (-1 point)\n\nI would much rather go to a Street food stall even though I have to suffer in the heat or with inadequate seating.\n\nOverall this restaurant has squandered the opportunity to present excellent Vietnamese food in a tasteful manner in a tasteful setting. A great disservice to Vietnam! (-1 point)\n\nFinally, pest control. Yes mosquitoes are an inevitability if you are not vigilant. While I was eating lunch, I also became lunch. (-1 point)\n\nOverall, with somewhere around 200-300 lunches consumed per year, I feel this time was not well used. I will not come back.\n\nReply to restaurant’s reply: this is a fair and balanced 1 star review.\n\nMy job in Vietnam is to find the people who care about this country and to demonstrate its greatness. I have to deeply understand dac san and the food, beverage and hospitality industries and lead the county to be respected because it can finally attain global standards.\n\nWhen you show an unrealistic example of your product and when the execution was never intended to be what you’re showing, then you make a fool of your customers and waste their time.\n\nFurther, whether this food is for me or not, the dishes are absolutely dishes I enjoy regularly and for my job I need to intimately understand this food. (Read: 600+ meals a year trying to understand dac san, service and the food beverage and hospitality industry here).\n\nYou’re in it for the money and misrepresentation is just theft. Places like this will destroy what’s left of this beautiful country.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 9, 2023",
